data: {"text":"1. That my client, M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd., is a private limited company duly incorporated"}

data: {"text":" under the Companies Act, 2013, having its registered office at [address], and is engaged in the business of construction and infrastructure"}

data: {"text":" development. My client is a reputable construction company with extensive experience in executing"}

data: {"text":" government projects and has been regularly undertaking construction works for various government departments and agencies across"}

data: {"text":" the State of Bihar.\n\n2. That my client was awarded the contract for construction of culverts on NH-31 vide Work Order No."}

data: {"text":" BRCD/PAT/2024/118 dated 12.06.2024 for a total contract value of Rs. 2,75,00,000/- (Rupees Two Crores"}

data: {"text":" Seventy Five Lakhs only). The said work order was issued by your office"}

data: {"text":" and my client duly accepted the same and commenced the construction work as"}

data: {"text":" per the terms and conditions stipulated therein.\n\n3. That my client executed the contracted work with"}

data: {"text":" utmost diligence and completed all the construction work of culverts on NH-31 by 28.02.2026 "}

data: {"text":"in accordance with the specifications and standards prescribed in the contract. Upon completion of the work, my client submitted the final running bills along with measurement books which"}

data: {"text":" were duly signed and verified by the site engineer appointed by your department, thereby acknowled"}

data: {"text":"ging the satisfactory completion of the contracted work.\n\n4. That despite the completion of work and submission of all requis"}

data: {"text":"ite documents, your office has wrongfully withheld the final payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- (Rupees Eighty Seven Lakhs Fifty Thousand only) which"}

data: {"text":" has remained outstanding since 28.02.2026. My client has made repeated requests and sent"}

data: {"text":" reminders dated 05.03.2026, 22.03.2026, and 18.04.2026 to your office for the release of the aforesaid amount, but no"}

data: {"text":" positive response has been received till date.\n\n5. That the wrongful withholding of the legitimate payment by your office has caused severe financial hardship to"}

data: {"text":" my client, affecting its cash flow and ability to meet its operational expenses and statutory obligations. Furthermore, the delay in payment"}

data: {"text":" has also caused reputational damage to my client in the construction industry and has adversely affected its business relationships"}

data: {"text":" with suppliers, sub-contractors, and financial institutions.\n\n6. That under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1"}

data: {"text":"908, no suit can be instituted against the Government or a public officer in"}

data: {"text":" respect of any act purporting to be done in official capacity without serving a notice of"}

data: {"text":" two months upon such Government or public officer. This notice is being"}

data: {"text":" served in compliance with the mandatory provisions of Section 80 CPC before instituting legal proceedings for"}

data: {"text":" recovery of the outstanding amount.\n\n7. That the withholding of payment without any justifiable reason constit"}

data: {"text":"utes a breach of contract and unjust enrichment on the part of the Government. My client is"}

data: {"text":" entitled to recover the outstanding amount along with interest and compensation for the losses suffered due to the in"}

data: {"text":"ordinate delay in payment.\n\n8. That you are hereby called upon to release the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,"}

data: {"text":"000/- along with applicable interest within a period of two months from the receipt of this notice, failing which my"}

data: {"text":" client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings for recovery of the said amount along with interest, damages"}

data: {"text":", and costs without any further reference to you."}

