data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"header","type":"template","content":"LEGAL NOTICE\n(Under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908)\n\nDate: 06 May 2026\n\nTo,\nThe Executive Engineer, Bihar Road Construction Department, Government of Bihar\nVishweshwaraiya Bhawan, Bailey Road, Patna - 800015\n\nFrom,\nM/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd.\nThrough: Adv. Anjali Verma, Advocate\nChamber No. 42, Patna High Court Bar Association, Patna - 800001","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"subject_line","type":"template","content":"Subject: Legal Notice under Section 80 CPC — prior to institution of suit against the Government / Public Officer\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nUnder instructions from and on behalf of my client, M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd., I hereby serve upon you this legal notice under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, and call upon you to note the following:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That my client, M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd., is a private limited company duly incorporated under the Companies Act, 2013, having its registered office at [address], and is engaged in the business of construction and infrastructure development. My client is a reputable construction company with extensive experience in executing government projects and has been regularly undertaking construction works for various government departments and agencies across the State of Bihar.\n\n2. That my client was awarded the contract for construction of culverts on NH-31 vide Work Order No. BRCD/PAT/2024/118 dated 12.06.2024 for a total contract value of Rs. 2,75,00,000/- (Rupees Two Crores Seventy Five Lakhs only). The said work order was issued by your office and my client duly accepted the same and commenced the construction work as per the terms and conditions stipulated therein.\n\n3. That my client executed the contracted work with utmost diligence and completed all the construction work of culverts on NH-31 by 28.02.2026 in accordance with the specifications and standards prescribed in the contract. Upon completion of the work, my client submitted the final running bills along with measurement books which were duly signed and verified by the site engineer appointed by your department, thereby acknowledging the satisfactory completion of the contracted work.\n\n4. That despite the completion of work and submission of all requisite documents, your office has wrongfully withheld the final payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- (Rupees Eighty Seven Lakhs Fifty Thousand only) which has remained outstanding since 28.02.2026. My client has made repeated requests and sent reminders dated 05.03.2026, 22.03.2026, and 18.04.2026 to your office for the release of the aforesaid amount, but no positive response has been received till date.\n\n5. That the wrongful withholding of the legitimate payment by your office has caused severe financial hardship to my client, affecting its cash flow and ability to meet its operational expenses and statutory obligations. Furthermore, the delay in payment has also caused reputational damage to my client in the construction industry and has adversely affected its business relationships with suppliers, sub-contractors, and financial institutions.\n\n6. That under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, no suit can be instituted against the Government or a public officer in respect of any act purporting to be done in official capacity without serving a notice of two months upon such Government or public officer. This notice is being served in compliance with the mandatory provisions of Section 80 CPC before instituting legal proceedings for recovery of the outstanding amount.\n\n7. That the withholding of payment without any justifiable reason constitutes a breach of contract and unjust enrichment on the part of the Government. My client is entitled to recover the outstanding amount along with interest and compensation for the losses suffered due to the inordinate delay in payment.\n\n8. That you are hereby called upon to release the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- along with applicable interest within a period of two months from the receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings for recovery of the said amount along with interest, damages, and costs without any further reference to you."},{"section_id":"demand_clause","type":"template","content":"DEMAND\n\nYou are hereby called upon to release the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from 28.02.2026 till actual payment, and pay damages of Rs. 5,00,000/- for the wrongful withholding within a period of two (2) months from the date of receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings before the competent civil court, at your risk, cost, and consequences, without any further reference to you.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"closing","type":"template","content":"A copy of this notice is retained in my office for record and further action.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n_________________________\nAdv. Anjali Verma\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. BCB/4521/2018\nChamber No. 42, Patna High Court Bar Association, Patna - 800001\n\n(Counsel for M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd.)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

